meta {
  name: Delete Deployment
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/deployments/{{deploymentId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Dev-User-ID: {{devUserId}}
}

docs {
  Initiates asynchronous teardown of a deployment. Returns 202 immediately after
  marking the row deleting; the orchestrator call and secret purge run in a background goroutine.

  Validation / behaviour:
    1. Authentication required.
    2. Parse deployment ID — 404 if not found.
    3. Deployer must own the deployment or be PlatformAdmin — 403 otherwise.
    4. If already deleted, returns 204 idempotently.
    5. Mark row state=deleting (synchronous).
    6. Background: Orchestrator.Delete removes the Argo CD Application; if Application is already
       gone it is treated as success.
    7. Background: SecretStore.DeleteAll purges every secret at kv/data/deployments/<id>/*.
    8. Background: Row soft-deleted and state set to deleted.
    9. Background: Write deployment.deleted to audit_logs.

  Responses:
    202 Accepted   — { id, state: "deleting" }
    204 No Content — deployment was already deleted (idempotent)
    401 unauthorized — unauthenticated
    403 forbidden  — caller does not own this deployment
    404 not_found  — deployment not found
}
